From 0749ed10b8cdd4a90653e7034446c5237e864637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sodhi, Vunny" <vunny.sodhi@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:11:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] maxim-serdes: max_des: guard NULL select_links op

max_des_select_links() unconditionally calls des->ops->select_links(),
but .select_links is an optional op. Some callers (e.g. ATR adapter
init and serializer address translation setup) reach this helper
without checking for it, which may dereference a NULL function
pointer on deserializers that do not implement it.

Return early when the op is not provided, matching the behavior of
the other call sites that already skip link selection in that case.

Signed-off-by: Sodhi, Vunny <vunny.sodhi@intel.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
index dc7af37249a2..ecc34ef1a1c5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
@@ -431,6 +431,9 @@ static int max_des_select_links(struct max_des_priv *priv, unsigned int mask)
 	struct max_des *des = priv->des;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!des->ops->select_links)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = des->ops->select_links(des, mask);
 	if (ret) {
 		priv->bound_link_mask_valid = false;
-- 
2.43.0

